# Gate step — data, not code (order 1072-b7eq). Wired by 1087-h2z9.
#
# Triaged from scripts/gate-divergence-declared.txt, where it sat `untriaged`
# since 2026-09-06: present in --ci-full, absent from --check, nobody decided.
# Measured green and cheap on b026372ff (Cheatsheet frontmatter), so the honest verdict is to run
# it where every host lands rather than once a day on the release gate.
#
# STEP_SCRIPT is a LITERAL path on purpose (1063-nraf): a binding assembled
# from a variable is invisible to every name-based scan. 1572-nqx5 ported the
# checker to Lua, so the binding is STEP_LUA; the ok line is byte-identical,
# so the regime pin below still quotes it.
STEP_DESC="Checking cheatsheet frontmatter"
STEP_LUA="scripts/lua/check-cheatsheet-frontmatter.lua"
STEP_ERROR="a cheatsheet has malformed frontmatter (1087-h2z9)"
STEP_OK="Cheatsheet frontmatter passed"
STEP_SECOND_REGIME="macneo 2026-09-22 darwin ok:cheatsheet-frontmatter:238"
